gae0(){return"I have read this and I accept how DesKilo handles my data."},
gae1(){return"Each space is run by its owner \u2014 your community \u2014 who decides members, prices and payment providers. Each server is run by its operator: the shared reference server by Florian Dittgen (Germany), a community's own server by whoever runs it. The app is free software (AGPL-3.0-or-later), published by Florian Dittgen. Online payments go through the provider the owner enabled (PayPal, Stripe, Mollie, Wero) under that provider's terms."},
gae2(){return"Who is responsible"},
gae3(){return"Before you use DesKilo, here is what the app does with your data, who can see it and what you can do about it. Two minutes; it is all there is."},
gae4(){return"Only the people in a conversation can open it: the two of you, the members of a group or, when you write to a space, the hosts the app names before you send. A space's owners and admins cannot read your conversations. Messages are not end-to-end encrypted: they are stored on the server the conversation lives on \u2014 another server's, after you confirm, when you write to someone there \u2014 and whoever runs that server can technically reach them."},
gae5(){return"Messages"},
gae6(){return"No tracking, no analytics, no advertising, no sale of data. Your data goes to nobody except the recipients named here and in the server's notice. The F-Droid build has no Google services at all."},
gae7(){return"What DesKilo never does"},
gae8(){return"Optional, and outbound. When the server's operator has set push up, your space uses it and it is on for this device, this device's address and each notification go to the push service (Firebase Cloud Messaging, which hands notifications for Apple devices on to Apple). A notification only says something generic, such as \"You have a new message\": no names, no times, no message text. Switch it off in Settings \u2192 Privacy & data; the app keeps working and nothing more is sent to this device."},
gae9(){return"Push notifications"},
gaea(){return"Read in the help"},
gaeb(){return"Read in the online guide"},
gaec(){return"As long as you are a member. When you leave a space and erase, your messages in that space go, and your profile goes with your last space. Accounting records stay for the legal retention period: the ledger by identifier, invoices as they were issued."},
gaed(){return"How long"},
gaee(){return"This text stays available in Settings \u2192 Privacy & data, in the in-app help (Privacy) and in the online user guide. A change of the text asks for your acceptance again."},
gaef(){return"The text you accepted, with the date \u2014 read it again anytime."},
gaeg(){return"Read it again anytime"},
gaeh(){return"Access, rectification, export (art. 20), erasure (art. 17) and objection \u2014 each is a button in Settings \u2192 Privacy & data. For anything else: fdittgen@gmail.com. You may withdraw this consent by leaving the workspace and erasing your data at any time."},
gaei(){return"Your rights"},
gFw(){return"Your data, your rights"},
gaej(){return"Your account could not be loaded, so there is nothing to accept yet."},
gO7(){return"Version"},
gaek(){return"Your account (e-mail, display name, hashed password), your profile as you fill it (photo, status, address, WhatsApp number \u2014 each optional), and what you do in a space: bookings and check-ins, messages, expenses and consumptions, your subscription, invoices and payments. All of it is stored on the server your space runs on: on the shared reference server, in the EU (Supabase, eu-central-1); on a server a community runs itself, wherever its operator chose. Settings \u2192 Privacy & data shows that server's notice: who runs it, where the data is and who receives it."},
gael(){return"What DesKilo processes"},
gaem(){return"Access follows roles and is enforced on the server: bookings are visible to the space (the floor plan shows occupancy); your finances and your commercial agreement only to you, the owners and the admins holding the matching permission. Each item of your profile is shown only to the audience you pick under Who sees me; nothing is public unless you choose it. A public profile stays off until you publish it: then anyone with the link reads your name, profession and bio \u2014 never your contact details, presence or spaces \u2014 until you withdraw it. Settings \u2192 Privacy & data names the people and lists who actually looked."},
